  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and customers pay for sales results, stock accuracy and reliable service. They judge you by field evidence and numbers, not by course names.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is knowing how much margin each step in the chain takes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and MBA in retail and FMCG management: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools forecast demand, suggest prices and draft reports. Routine reporting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Field relationships, judgment in messy situations and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for analysis; later, own decisions on range, price and people.
  </p>

